Subject: [#94-8-76] Reincarnation, immortality and cryonic suspension

One of the deficiencies I see with some arrangements is that they keep no 
records of reanimation desires.  I have arrangements with Alcor, and have never 
been asked for "reanimation preferences."  When reanimation become feasible, we 
will have to make decisions about when to reanimate people.

When do extropians want to be reanimated?:

1. When the cause of their death is cured, but old age has not been cured.
2. When reanimation is possible, aging is cured, but uploading is not possible.
3. When reanimation is possible, old age is cured, and uploading is possible.
4. When reanimation is 25% successful.  50%?  90%?  99%?
5. When reanimation is possible, but not with the same body.
6. When reanimation is possible, but only with the same body.
7. When reanimation is possible, but with side-effects.
8. When reanimation is possible for you, but not your life-partner yet.
9. When reanimation is possible, but only by assuming a massive debt.
10. When reanimation is possible, but society considers your religion/sexual 
preference/radical politics to be criminal, and you will be sentenced to life 
imprisonment upon reanimation.
11. When reanimation is possible, but a desired goal (space travel, money fund 
peaks, etc.) has not yet occurred.
